oes: comprise/1

# Mozilla as a public sample Holotype (phase 7 prototype), built on 2026-10-18 from public sources only: the Foundation's Forms 990 and audited
# statements, the Mozilla wiki and blog, each organization's own pages, Companies House, GitHub and reputable reporting. No person is named
# anywhere; seats are roles and E is none in every atom. Every node cites its sources by URL; a fact no current source confirms is a pending
# question, never a guess. Facts change. A third-party description, reviewed by nobody at Mozilla.
#
# Atoms: the Foundation (the perspective), Mozilla.org (the umbrella non-profit the Foundation controls, which per its June 2026 FAQ owns the
# operating companies), the Corporation (Firefox), MZLA (Thunderbird), Mozilla.ai, Mozilla Ventures and Mozilla Data Collective.
# The ownership of the companies is stated differently by Mozilla's own pages (the 2024 filings and the State of Mozilla 2025/26: the Foundation;
# the FAQ of June 2026 and the Thunderbird pages: Mozilla.org). The model follows the newest source and says so in the bonds and the findings.

id: holotype/mozilla
name: Mozilla
sample: true
summary: The Mozilla Foundation and the Mozilla organizations around it (Mozilla.org, the Corporation, MZLA, Mozilla.ai, Mozilla Ventures, Mozilla Data Collective), from public sources only.
alignment:                 # whose company this is, as the people who made it said; a claim, never proof (plan/standing.md)
  for: other
  mode: research
  by: "comprise-sample"
  at: 2026-10-18
atoms:
  - atom/mozilla-foundation
  - atom/mozilla-org
  - atom/mozilla-corporation
  - atom/mzla
  - atom/mozilla-ai
  - atom/mozilla-ventures
  - atom/mozilla-data-collective
perspective: atom/mozilla-foundation

# Every source a node cites, by its URL (the id is the URL, so `provenance.sources` reads as links). Read on 2026-10-18.
sources:
  - id: https://stateof.mozilla.org/pdf/Mozilla%20Foundation_Form_990_2024.pdf
    page: Mozilla Foundation, IRS Form 990 for 2024 (public disclosure copy, signed 2025-11-17), with Schedules O and R
    supports: EIN, mission, governance counts, Foundation-only revenue and expenses, program expenses, Schedule R related organizations with EINs, ownership, income and assets, and transactions with them
    date: 2026-10-18
  - id: https://assets.mozilla.net/annualreport/2024/b200-mozilla-foundation-form-990-public-disclosure-ty23.pdf
    page: Mozilla Foundation, IRS Form 990 for 2023 (public disclosure copy), Schedule R
    supports: Related organizations and their 2023 income and assets; 2023 transactions with the Corporation and the fund
    date: 2026-10-18
  - id: https://stateof.mozilla.org/pdf/Mozilla%20Fdn%202024%20-%20AuditedFinancials.pdf
    page: Mozilla Foundation and Subsidiaries, consolidated financial statements for 2024 and 2023 (audited; issued 2025-09-26)
    supports: Wholly-owned subsidiaries, consolidated revenue by source, expenses, net assets, trademark licence fees, services agreements, acquisitions, the Mozilla Online dispute, subsequent events
    date: 2026-10-18
  - id: https://projects.propublica.org/nonprofits/organizations/200097189
    page: 'ProPublica Nonprofit Explorer: Mozilla Foundation (EIN 20-0097189), Form 990 filings 2011 to 2024'
    supports: EIN, ruling year 2004, NTEE class, revenue, expenses and net assets by year
    date: 2026-10-18
  - id: https://projects.propublica.org/nonprofits/api/v2/organizations/200097189.json
    page: ProPublica Nonprofit Explorer API record for Mozilla Foundation
    supports: Address, NTEE code U40, ruling date 2004-06, total assets and liabilities by year
    date: 2026-10-18
  - id: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mozilla_Foundation
    page: 'Wikipedia: Mozilla Foundation'
    supports: Formation date, California registration number, subsidiaries announced and dates, the November 2024 layoffs (secondary source)
    date: 2026-10-18
  - id: https://wiki.mozilla.org/Mozilla_org
    page: 'Mozilla wiki: Mozilla.org, the FAQ on the new nonprofit (last edited 2026-06-23)'
    supports: What Mozilla.org is, that it owns the operating subsidiaries and the trademarks, that the Foundation appoints the majority of its board and consolidates it, the councils, the 2026 to 2028 strategy
    date: 2026-10-18
  - id: https://blog.mozilla.org/en/mozilla/news/announcing-mozilla-org-new-non-profit/
    page: 'Mozilla blog: Announcing Mozilla.org (2026-06-23)'
    supports: Mozilla.org as a 501(c)(3) strategic endowment operating the portfolio on behalf of the Foundation
    date: 2026-10-18
  - id: https://www.mofo.com/resources/news/260706-mofo-advises-mozilla
    page: Law firm press release on advising on the creation of Mozilla.org (2026-07-06)
    supports: Mozilla.org granted 501(c)(3) status and operational in June 2026; the list of organizations in the Mozilla Project
    date: 2026-10-18
  - id: https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/about/governance/organizations/
    page: 'Mozilla: Organizations (governance page, undated; still says the Foundation wholly owns the Corporation)'
    supports: Foundation as California non-profit; Corporation as its wholly owned taxable subsidiary; Mozilla Online as a Corporation subsidiary
    date: 2026-10-18
  - id: https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/about/
    page: 'Mozilla: About (2026)'
    supports: The Mozilla Project and its organizations; product and program list
    date: 2026-10-18
  - id: https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/about/leadership/
    page: 'Mozilla: Leadership (2026), role titles only used'
    supports: Role titles across the family and the named boards
    date: 2026-10-18
  - id: https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/about/manifesto/
    page: The Mozilla Manifesto
    supports: The ten principles
    date: 2026-10-18
  - id: https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/foundation/trademarks/policy/
    page: Mozilla trademark policy (undated)
    supports: Names the Mozilla Foundation as owner of the Mozilla marks
    date: 2026-10-18
  - id: https://stateof.mozilla.org/
    page: State of Mozilla 2025/26
    supports: Structure as the Foundation describes it; the three principles; links to the 2024 filings
    date: 2026-10-18
  - id: https://stateof.mozilla.org/ledger/
    page: 'State of Mozilla 2025/26: Ledger'
    supports: Reserves, 2026 planned spend and its split, Firefox-related income 2024, 50+ equity holdings, the double bottom line
    date: 2026-10-18
  - id: https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/foundation/annualreport/2024/
    page: 'State of Mozilla 2024: contents'
    supports: The report groups Mozilla VPN, Monitor and Relay as products built for people; lists Mozilla Builders, Mozilla Advertising and the other entities
    date: 2026-10-18
  - id: https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/foundation/annualreport/2024/article/financing-an-open-internet-mozillas-path-forward/
    page: 'State of Mozilla 2024: Financing an open internet'
    supports: Foundation as sole owner of the Corporation; search partnerships as the majority of revenue; Mozilla Ventures fund size and deployment; MZLA donations; Mozilla.ai commitment
    date: 2026-10-18
  - id: https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/foundation/annualreport/2024/article/backing-bold-ideas-mozilla-venturesa-and-responsible-innovation/
    page: 'State of Mozilla 2024: Backing bold ideas (Mozilla Ventures)'
